[manpage_begin nsstats n 1.15]
[moddesc {NaviServer External Modules}]
[titledesc {Monitoring and statistics web interface}]
[description]
The nsstats module provides an administrative web interface for NaviServer.
It displays process information, virtual-server configuration, connection pools,
network drivers, background jobs, memory, caches, shared variables and logs.
Features are detected at runtime so older supported NaviServer releases remain usable.

[section INSTALLATION]
Place [file nsstats.tcl] and [file nsstats.adp] in an administrative page directory.
Configure access control before exposing these pages. OpenACS installations can
use their protected administration directory. The module Makefile installs the
pages and its parameter dictionary; no documentation rendering is required by
an ordinary installation.

[section DIAGNOSTICS]
When the core [cmd ns_stats] command is available, ready shared samples provide
interval rates and timing averages. The utilization page shows sampling age and
interval and permits selecting a live snapshot. History uses SQLite persistence
when configured, or the bounded in-memory sample buffer. Charts break across gaps
and restarts; missing values remain unknown. Sampling and persistence are configured
in the process-wide [const ns/stats] section, independently of this web interface.
Older installations retain the original collectors.

[para]
The parameter reference loads the core dictionary and available installed module
dictionaries. The MCP administration page appears when nsmcp is active; inspection
calls require an explicit administrator action and use the normal protocol checks.

